infrastructure/terraform/*.tfstate*
infrastructure/terraform/.terraform.lock.hcl
# main.tf's backend "s3" block holds the real state bucket name + DynamoDB
# lock table when used locally. Committed version must have CHANGEME-
# placeholders — so we gitignore this file entirely to prevent accidental
# leak into the public OS repo. If you need to commit changes to other parts
# of main.tf, force-add it with CHANGEME- placeholders restored, then put
# the real backend values back afterwards.
infrastructure/terraform/main.tf

# YOLO model WEIGHTS (large binary files). ANCHORED to the repo root — the weights live in
# /models (yolo_*.pt, tatr/model.safetensors); build-artifact copies under .next are covered
# by the .next ignore. The previous UN-anchored `models/` glob also matched the SOURCE route
# dir src/app/api/admin/models/, leaving admin/models/route.ts + models/reprocess-csi/route.ts
# UNTRACKED (fresh clones/CI/deploy were missing them). Weight leaks are additionally blocked
# by the CloudFront + task-role Deny rules (defense-in-depth). [refactor jul6 S041 — S001-class
# tree-integrity gap]
/models/

# internal planning docs — ANCHORED to repo root (DR004 TREE-1/TREE-2): un-anchored dir/file
# globs are the same antipattern that gitignored the admin/models SOURCE dir (S041). These
# only ignore the root-level planning docs; a same-named source file under src/ stays tracked.
# (NOTE: *.plan / *.pem below stay UN-anchored ON PURPOSE — secret/key protection must match
# at any depth.)
/plans/
/REFACTORED_MARCH29.md
/bucket-fill.md
/csv-editor-panel.md
/symbol-search-fix.md

